352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (We believe in adhering strictly to the biblical injunction to be controlled by the Holy Spirit in both our thoughts and behaviors \(Romans 8:9, Romans 12:2\). While some theological positions may advocate for the permissibility of alcohol consumption, we recognize the pervasive societal struggle with alcoholism and addiction. In light of this, we maintain our stance against all forms of alcohol consumption primarily with our Pastoral Team, Staff and Board Members.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
353 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (While acknowledging differing interpretations, we firmly believe that a life of sobriety is overwhelmingly advocated for in the Bible - especially for the betterment and example of those in our community who have come out of a life of addiction and abuse. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
354 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (We believe that embracing sobriety aligns us more closely with the teachings of Jesus Christ and enables us to better fulfill our mission to serve and support one another in faith. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
